# Web Frontend Rules

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router
- React 19
- Tailwind CSS 4
- MapLibre GL via `maplibre-gl`
- Custom shadcn-style UI components in `components/ui`

## UI Conventions

- Keep the home screen full-height and map-first.
- Use airy spacing, rounded surfaces, and soft glass panels from `app/globals.css`.
- Primary CTA stays singular and visually dominant.
- Modal card is the main detail surface; avoid creating competing side panels in the MVP.
- The map should prefer Russian/local labels, stable tile loading, and minimal overlay clutter.

## SEO Conventions

- In `view` mode, role/type must render as technical `<h1>`.
- In `view` mode, breed must render as technical `<h2>`.
- Edit/create mode can use non-heading text for the shell title.

## Safety Conventions

- Only allow VK Video and RuTube URLs to become iframe embeds.
- Do not render arbitrary iframe sources.
- Document links must stay `http/https` only.
- Demo gallery previews should use supported HTTPS image hosts to avoid runtime failures with image optimization rules.

## State Conventions

- Server page resolves initial query params.
- Client shell owns selected pin, draft pin, and URL synchronization.
- Use key-based remounting for modal reset when opening another pin or switching between create/view flows.
- Keep custom map markers and source badge aligned with the current raster tile provider.

## Styling Tokens

- Accent: `--accent`
- Accent hover: `--accent-hover`
- Accent subtle: `--accent-subtle`
- Text primary: `--text-primary`
- Text secondary: `--text-secondary`
- Border: `--border`
- Surface shadows: `--shadow-sm`, `--shadow-md`, `--shadow-lg`
